=====WATCHBILL=====
{
  "watch1": {
    "scenarios": [
      "features/todo-dom-stability.feature:Completing a todo keeps the same element in the DOM",
      "features/todo-dom-stability.feature:Uncompleting a todo keeps the same element in the DOM"
    ]
  },
  "watch2": {
    "scenarios": [
      "features/todo-dom-stability.feature:The completion-toggle seams do not rebuild the list on a same-visibility toggle"
    ]
  }
}

=====PACKAGE=====
{
  "name": "todomvc-shakedown",
  "version": "0.1.0",
  "private": true,
  "scripts": { "test": "cucumber-js" },
  "devDependencies": { "@cucumber/cucumber": "*", "happy-dom": "*" }
}

=====README=====
# TodoMVC (shakedown build)

A TodoMVC app to be built following `assets/app-spec.md`, using
`assets/app-template.index.html` as the base markup. Vanilla JS, no preprocessors.
The test runner is Cucumber (see package.json); write DOM-level scenarios under
`features/` and step definitions under `features/support/`.

Verification support ships with the project: `features/support/world.js` loads the REAL
`index.html` and `js/app.js` into a happy-dom window before every scenario, and exposes
`this.document` / `this.window`. Drive the app through those; do not build a DOM by hand.

=====GITIGNORE=====
node_modules

=====DOM-STABILITY FEATURE=====
Feature: Todo list element stability
  As a todo-list user
  I want the app to update an item without replacing its list element
  So that a browser that already holds a reference to that element keeps working after I change its state

  Rule: The app mutates an existing list element in place when an item's completion changes, instead of rebuilding the list

  Scenario: Completing a todo keeps the same element in the DOM
    Given the app loads with active todo "a"
    And I hold a reference to the todo "a" element
    When I complete the todo "a"
    Then the todo "a" element is the same element as the held reference

  Scenario: Uncompleting a todo keeps the same element in the DOM
    Given the app loads with completed todo "a"
    And I hold a reference to the todo "a" element
    When I complete the todo "a"
    Then the todo "a" element is the same element as the held reference

  Rule: The completion-toggle seams preserve the toggled element's identity by construction

  @conformance
  Scenario: The completion-toggle seams do not rebuild the list on a same-visibility toggle
    Given the completion-toggle source in "js/app.js"
    When the structural conformance check inspects the completeTodo and toggleAllTodos seams
    Then neither seam rebuilds the todo list when a completion toggle leaves the item visible
    And each seam mutates the toggled list element's completed class and its toggle checked state in place

  Rule: While a todo is being edited, its label control is hidden

  Scenario: Editing a todo hides its label
    Given the app loads with todo "a"
    When I double-click the label of the todo "a"
    Then the label of the todo "a" is not visible

=====SUPPORT DIR=====
